# {{project_name}} — Claude Code entry point

@AGENTS.md

The bare line above is an IMPORT, and it has to stay bare. Claude Code expands
`@path` and nothing else — a markdown link to the same file is inert prose, so
the canonical instructions stay unread while this file goes on shadowing the
native `AGENTS.md` path Claude Code would otherwise have used. That is what this
template shipped until 2026-09-21, and the cost was measured: across six
scaffolded repositories, 45,720 bytes of canonical instructions never reached a
single session. Wrapping the import in backticks or a fenced block disables it
the same way.

`AGENTS.md` is the Linux Foundation standard file most coding agents read
natively, and it is the source of truth for workflow, conventions, memory, tools
and branch naming. Its "Claude Code specifics" section applies to this session.
Anything Claude-only belongs below the import, never inside `AGENTS.md`.

